# Settings Compose itself reads (copy to .env). They choose host paths and devices.
#
# The PTT interface is found as /dev/moreopenrepeater-ptt, a name a udev rule makes on the host so it
# survives the hidraw number changing (sudo cp udev/61-moreopenrepeater-ptt.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/, then
# sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=hidraw --action=add).
# Only set this to use a particular node instead (check: ls -l /dev/hidraw*), which will not follow a renumbering.
# MOR_PTT_HIDRAW=/dev/hidraw0
# The host's gpio group number (check: getent group gpio)
# MOR_GPIO_GID=986
# Where the saved configuration lives on the host
# MOR_DATA_DIR=./data
# Where the dashboard is published on the host: loopback until you have an account (see compose.yaml).
# MOR_API_HOST=127.0.0.1
# MOR_API_PORT=8000
# The private network the services share (default 172.28.0.0/24), and the fixed addresses of the core and the AllStar
# node in it. Change the subnet if it clashes with a network you use, and keep the addresses inside it.
# MOR_SERVICES_SUBNET=172.28.0.0/24
# MOR_CORE_IP=172.28.0.10
# MOR_ALLSTAR_IP=172.28.0.20
# The host port IAX2 (AllStarLink node to node) is published on. The default is the one AllStarLink uses.
# MOR_ALLSTAR_IAX_PORT=4569
# The DMR bridge's fixed address on the private network (the core only hears its audio from this address). Keep it inside
# MOR_SERVICES_SUBNET.
# MOR_DMR_IP=172.28.0.30
